---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ConceptDiagram from "../../components/ConceptDiagram.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="About">
  <section class="hero container prose">
    <h1>About K8s Practice Lab</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      A complete learning environment for <strong>containers and Kubernetes</strong> —
      browser-based lessons plus optional real cluster practice on localhost.
    </p>

    <h2>Three modes, one repo</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Browser</strong> — 7 modules, quizzes, simulated kubectl (no install)</li>
      <li><strong>Localhost</strong> — kind cluster + guided labs with real YAML</li>
      <li><strong>AWS</strong> — optional Terraform to host the site on S3 + CloudFront</li>
    </ul>

    <ConceptDiagram />

    <h2>Simulation vs real clusters</h2>
    <p>
      The simulator teaches <em>what</em> commands do and <em>why</em>. The local kind cluster
      gives you the real feel — latency, port-forwards, actual logs. Use both.
    </p>

    <h2>Built in public</h2>
    <p>
      Open source on <a href="https://github.com/Jacob-Idolor/Pet_Projects">GitHub</a>.
      Fork it, run <code>make local-lab</code>, host your own copy on AWS, improve it, share it.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
